From af20c3d177db39b6b994c79064140d4d01fc3a84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gerege Systems Development Team <dev@gerege.mn>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 10:29:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] feat(modules): move all remaining business-module wiring
 out of server.go

Phase 1 near-complete: ai (incl. public chat, knowledge warm-up, own rate
limiters), sign (incl. signer material loading, publishes ServiceSign for
App.Sign()), gov + relay (with SLA sweep / demo simulator as registered
background workers), registry (+catalog), applications and gateway-console
now assemble themselves in modules/<id>/module.go.

Host gains optional capabilities: Provide (modules publish services back -
admin route consumes the ai usecase this way), AddWorker (module background
jobs started by App.Run) and OnShutdown (limiter cleanup). App drops the
signUC/relayUC/govUC/aiRateLimiter fields in favour of module-registered
services/workers/shutdown hooks.

Only auth/users/rbac/org/audit/site/superadmin/assets (core) and the deeply
OIDC-coupled provider/eidproxy wiring remain inline. Golden route inventory
is byte-identical - no behaviour change.
